From eb1da9efd3e62366ae6f446e213eeec2069dcb68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <16584630+hfyeomans@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:15:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LLAMA_MOE_HOT_MAP: a layer's busiest experts pinned in the
 MoE cache and kept out of host memory

A map names, per layer, the experts the layer's card pins.  The layer's experts are loaded in a new order with those last: host
memory holds only the others, the MoE cache reads the pinned ones from the model file into the first slots of the layer's own
group and never gives them up.  The router's rows take the same order, so the model computes the same thing.
LLAMA_MOE_HOT_VERIFY=1 compares the host experts, the router rows and the pinned slots with the model file at start.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a1dcf3-98bb-7200-b1a5-d8e1c956fb0c
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
